WEBVTT

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:07.988
Appearing unexpectedly, almost like a
magician, Patricia's grandmother...

00:00:08.023 --> 00:00:12.880
...managed to tightly bind Candy's
and Patricia's hearts together.

00:00:13.925 --> 00:00:17.627
Now that grandmother Marhsa is gone,
the dorm suddenly feels lonely.

00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:21.273
Life has returned to normal.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:29.600
The inverted envelope.

00:00:38.845 --> 00:00:41.175
-I'm done!
-Candice!

00:00:45.031 --> 00:00:48.634
-Yeah, I can't get up before
everybody is done eating...

00:00:48.695 --> 00:00:52.738
-She doesn't know anything!
-As expected from a barn dogsbody!

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.974
Why are they eating like that?
Maybe the food is no good?

00:01:06.038 --> 00:01:08.322
What a waste, she left so much!

00:01:11.177 --> 00:01:14.338
-Just take a look at that.
-She would've choked on it.

00:01:19.138 --> 00:01:23.460
Everyone, you're done, aren't you?
Let's thank God for this meal.

00:01:31.303 --> 00:01:33.303
Now I'll hand out the mail you received.

00:01:33.949 --> 00:01:36.089
-Patricia O'Brien!
-Yes!

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:42.733
Eliza Leagan!
-Yes!

00:01:42.738 --> 00:01:48.661
-Wow, so many!
-It'll be a lot of work answering all of these!

00:01:48.919 --> 00:01:50.517
That's great!

00:01:51.612 --> 00:01:53.292
Archibald Cornwell!

00:01:53.999 --> 00:01:56.487
This letter should've been delivered
to boys' ward.

00:01:56.763 --> 00:02:02.354
-Teacher, can I go and deliver it then?
-No, I'll deliver it later on.

00:02:03.679 --> 00:02:05.906
Candice White Adley.

00:02:06.646 --> 00:02:07.773
For me?

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:12.888
It's from America!
It's from sister Pony!

00:02:13.802 --> 00:02:17.749
-It even smells like American land!
-Candice!

00:02:20.036 --> 00:02:22.055
-I have to read it right now!

00:02:23.142 --> 00:02:26.175
-Candice, you mustn't run!
-Oops.

00:02:36.528 --> 00:02:40.553
Candy, I'm sure you'll begin enjoying
your days in London...

00:02:40.588 --> 00:02:43.712
...as soon as you get used
to the new kind of life.

00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:49.878
Sister Lane and I are spending our
days looking after children.

00:02:49.993 --> 00:02:55.776
Speaking of kids, now that the spring
had come, so many animals have been born.

00:02:56.008 --> 00:03:01.836
All at once, we got six chicks and
seven piglets.

00:03:01.871 --> 00:03:03.835
Everyone was thrilled!

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.699
That's so cute!

00:03:14.867 --> 00:03:16.090
Eliza?

00:03:17.327 --> 00:03:21.800
-Why, this is a weird envelope.
-What are you doing? Give it back!

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:25.523
Hey, there is something written
on the inside of the envelope.

00:03:25.558 --> 00:03:30.334
-Really, that's a weird envelope!
-I said, give it back!

00:03:30.464 --> 00:03:35.119
Receiving a letter in an inverted, old envelope...
Exactly what I'd expect from you, Candy.

00:03:35.306 --> 00:03:37.241
You've been using this ever since
you transferred?

00:03:39.722 --> 00:03:44.080
-Pony's home is so poor!
-Eliza!

00:03:48.185 --> 00:03:49.811
What a violent person!

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:54.153
Why would reusing an old evnelope
be so bad?

00:03:54.256 --> 00:03:55.317
That's enough!

00:03:56.231 --> 00:03:58.419
Where do you think you are?

00:04:01.031 --> 00:04:03.307
Teacher, Candy was violent!

00:04:06.020 --> 00:04:07.197
I saw it.

00:04:08.626 --> 00:04:11.207
-Did she hurt you, Eliza?
-Nah...

00:04:11.621 --> 00:04:15.762
Teacher, I don't want to live with
such a volatile person!

00:04:15.797 --> 00:04:17.893
That's right. She's a bad person.

00:04:19.897 --> 00:04:24.452
Taking and reading other people's mail,
and then using it for a prank, is much worse!

00:04:24.610 --> 00:04:26.397
That's not what a lady would've done!

00:04:28.888 --> 00:04:30.086
Teacher...

00:04:32.907 --> 00:04:35.159
All of you, return to your rooms!

00:04:41.660 --> 00:04:44.892
-Candy!
-Thanks!

00:04:48.178 --> 00:04:51.682
That's horrible! Candy even turned
a teacher into her ally!

00:04:53.116 --> 00:04:55.111
Do you think I'll leave it like this?

00:04:55.322 --> 00:04:56.960
What will you do, Eliza?

00:04:58.496 --> 00:05:01.256
Tomorrow, after the morning prayer...

00:05:13.271 --> 00:05:14.354
Candy?

00:05:15.814 --> 00:05:16.954
It's Eliza.

00:05:17.794 --> 00:05:20.392
Maybe she's discussing
a new prank with her brother.

00:05:22.512 --> 00:05:24.775
-I'm afraid.
-It's okay!

00:05:24.810 --> 00:05:26.134
Pretend you didn't see them.

00:05:32.790 --> 00:05:35.492
Hey, Candy!
I want to talk to you.

00:05:35.903 --> 00:05:38.820
-Candy!
-It's okay! Go ahead, Patty.

00:05:43.244 --> 00:05:44.971
Now, let's go, Patty.

00:05:51.184 --> 00:05:54.215
Let go...
Let go of my arm!

00:05:54.773 --> 00:05:56.356
I can walk on my own.

00:05:56.606 --> 00:05:58.175
What did you want to talk about, Neil?

00:05:59.269 --> 00:06:01.187
Long time no see.

00:06:01.222 --> 00:06:04.085
I really didn't think I'd find
you here in London.

00:06:04.086 --> 00:06:06.777
Really! I'm pretty disappointed though!

00:06:06.812 --> 00:06:09.784
You're still trailing along with your sister.
Even to this place!

00:06:10.365 --> 00:06:11.929
What was that?

00:06:13.277 --> 00:06:17.059
Neil, you're still a wimpy show-off,
even here in London.

00:06:17.276 --> 00:06:18.495
Damn...!

00:06:19.486 --> 00:06:20.346
Hey!

00:06:27.734 --> 00:06:30.863
I had a hunch that something was up!

00:06:30.898 --> 00:06:34.279
You still haven't changed your
habit of crying for help!

00:06:34.486 --> 00:06:35.913
You've got some nerve!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:38.856
I think your clothes are turned
inside-out, Candy!

00:06:41.487 --> 00:06:44.275
You like it when things are
inside-out, don't you?

00:06:47.991 --> 00:06:49.308
I'll check it out!

00:06:50.318 --> 00:06:51.454
You're kidding me!

00:06:52.586 --> 00:06:53.486
That girl!

00:06:53.802 --> 00:06:55.056
What are you doing?

00:06:57.719 --> 00:06:58.821
Stand still!

00:07:03.405 --> 00:07:04.706
Ow! What are you doing?

00:07:04.914 --> 00:07:07.842
She's built up some muscle
from working the stables!

00:07:08.025 --> 00:07:10.046
Ow! Let go of me!

00:07:10.206 --> 00:07:14.815
-We want to see you cry!
-We'll let you go if you cry!

00:07:15.184 --> 00:07:16.838
Let go of me!

00:07:18.667 --> 00:07:20.419
Cry! Now!

00:07:23.056 --> 00:07:26.644
This school is not for your kind!

00:07:30.613 --> 00:07:32.841
But it's okay for my kind?

00:07:33.879 --> 00:07:35.824
Right, boy?

00:07:36.409 --> 00:07:37.496
Terry!

00:07:39.332 --> 00:07:42.083
I think I heard you saying "you're free to stay".

00:07:46.257 --> 00:07:47.397
Well then?

00:07:48.666 --> 00:07:49.805
Please do...

00:07:50.781 --> 00:07:55.238
I see. You said it because I'm the
oldest son of an eminent English nobleman.

00:07:57.357 --> 00:07:58.545
Y... yes...

00:08:00.353 --> 00:08:02.500
Are rich people really so admirable?

00:08:07.182 --> 00:08:11.373
So three rich Americans are
messing around a single girl?

00:08:11.841 --> 00:08:17.963
Of course. In that case, I'll teach you
everything about kind ways of English aristocracy!

00:08:23.884 --> 00:08:25.122
Get out of here!

00:08:25.726 --> 00:08:27.768
I'll remember this!

00:08:37.584 --> 00:08:40.584
Hey...
Wait!

00:08:43.145 --> 00:08:44.347
Can I help you?

00:08:45.083 --> 00:08:48.327
Thank you...
I... I...

00:08:49.235 --> 00:08:53.305
You don't need to thank me.
Besides, I wasn't trying to protect you.

00:08:55.195 --> 00:08:58.938
I loathe their kind.
That's pretty much it.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:10.066
Why are you looking at me like that?

00:09:10.190 --> 00:09:13.414
Want to confess your love, Lady freckles?

00:09:15.228 --> 00:09:17.171
Lady freckles?

00:09:17.983 --> 00:09:20.833
He remembers what happened on the ship.

00:09:21.507 --> 00:09:25.994
He remembers... and yet, he's been
ignoring me the whole time!

00:09:27.851 --> 00:09:30.219
I know of an ideal place
for love confessions!

00:09:30.359 --> 00:09:31.208
Want to come?

00:09:31.445 --> 00:09:33.774
Who'd want to say that?

00:09:34.147 --> 00:09:39.302
Thank goodness. I'm sorry, but I'm
not interested in freckled girls.

00:09:39.466 --> 00:09:40.552
Well then, excuse me.

00:09:44.374 --> 00:09:47.916
What's up with that, I just wanted to
express my sincere gratitude to him!

00:09:52.547 --> 00:09:57.395
And my name isn't Lady freckles!
It's Candice White Adley!

00:10:13.993 --> 00:10:17.188
I have too much to write about,
the letter won't turn out okay...

00:10:21.268 --> 00:10:22.270
Terry!

00:10:23.981 --> 00:10:26.636
Who'd write about that guy, anyway?

00:10:26.671 --> 00:10:28.753
He's a whimsical snob.. I hate him!

00:10:29.742 --> 00:10:32.343
*Denjin Anime Fansub*
what

00:10:33.663 --> 00:10:35.625
Yes, come in!

00:10:39.228 --> 00:10:40.344
Patty!

00:10:40.379 --> 00:10:44.845
Uh, after the prayer, a guy with glasses
approached me with this...

00:10:45.778 --> 00:10:47.991
It's Stear, right?
Thank you!

00:10:48.423 --> 00:10:49.593
I wonder what it's about.

00:10:51.178 --> 00:10:52.621
What is this?

00:10:53.877 --> 00:10:55.357
Take a look, Patty.

00:10:55.392 --> 00:10:58.064
No...! Reading other people's letters...

00:10:58.998 --> 00:11:01.101
I don't think you could really
call it a letter...

00:11:01.302 --> 00:11:02.603
It's a code of some kind.

00:11:02.802 --> 00:11:04.298
In that case, excuse me...

00:11:04.965 --> 00:11:07.081
It's Morse code!

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:11.826
-What, this is what they use in telegraphy?
-Yes.

00:11:18.884 --> 00:11:20.258
It's Stear!

00:11:20.577 --> 00:11:22.889
I see, he's signalling me with lights...

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:27.283
This was... E...
Uh, Patty, what is he saying?

00:11:28.109 --> 00:11:35.577
-Chi...o..ko...re...to...ari...
-They have chocolate?

00:11:35.612 --> 00:11:42.678
-Ku...ri...n...mo...
-Kurin is with them, too?

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:51.059
-o...i...de...ko...u...
-They're telling me to come over?

00:11:53.646 --> 00:11:54.757
Alright!

00:11:58.469 --> 00:12:00.046
Say, Patty, won't you come along?

00:12:00.757 --> 00:12:02.378
Where to?

00:12:03.729 --> 00:12:05.705
Of course, to boys' ward!

00:12:05.845 --> 00:12:09.039
God won't forgive us if we do that!

00:12:11.257 --> 00:12:15.349
-It's so late, God already went to bed!
-What are you going to do?

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:19.585
Patty, it might be too difficult for you.
I'll bring you some chocolate however!

00:12:28.418 --> 00:12:30.104
Ca... Candy!

00:12:30.484 --> 00:12:31.748
I'm off!

00:12:46.664 --> 00:12:48.144
Candy, is that you?

00:12:52.751 --> 00:12:54.328
Good evening, Archie!

00:12:54.955 --> 00:12:59.478
-Take care, Candy!
-Don't worry! I'm used to high places!

00:13:06.191 --> 00:13:07.196
Are you okay?

00:13:10.976 --> 00:13:12.478
I'm okay, Kurin.

00:13:12.513 --> 00:13:15.230
I haven't climbed a tree in a long time,
I must've gotten rusty...

00:13:15.265 --> 00:13:17.430
Now, hurry inside! We'll get in trouble
if they find you here.

00:13:21.007 --> 00:13:23.180
Kurin, long time no see...

00:13:26.503 --> 00:13:29.149
-I wanted to see you!
-Welcome, Candy!

00:13:30.518 --> 00:13:32.051
Where are you, Stear?

00:13:32.086 --> 00:13:33.892
I'm here... up here.

00:13:34.315 --> 00:13:35.637
S.. Stear!

00:13:38.446 --> 00:13:42.469
Candy, my new invention, spider shoes.

00:13:42.728 --> 00:13:44.602
Incredible, what an invention!

00:13:47.052 --> 00:13:49.972
Well there you have my brother...
I can't look at this anymore...

00:13:50.007 --> 00:13:52.918
I can walk on the ceiling...
Even Edison didn't think of this!

00:13:55.853 --> 00:13:58.074
Can I borrow them sometime?

00:13:58.491 --> 00:14:00.214
Okay... Now if I do this, uh...

00:14:09.483 --> 00:14:12.178
The problem is that they're
pretty unreliable.

00:14:14.096 --> 00:14:17.208
I'll improve them by the next time...

00:14:18.255 --> 00:14:19.750
I can't wait to see them!

00:14:20.239 --> 00:14:22.621
-Would you like some tea?
-Allow me!

00:14:26.121 --> 00:14:29.395
Say, who is in the next room?

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:30.925
One nasty dude.

00:14:30.960 --> 00:14:34.527
It's the guy who made an incident
during the prayer.

00:14:38.725 --> 00:14:39.797
Terry?

00:14:40.958 --> 00:14:43.184
That's right, Grandchester Terrius!

00:14:43.278 --> 00:14:46.828
One day, he and Archie almost had a fight
in the main hall.

00:14:47.024 --> 00:14:48.533
Archie?

00:14:49.161 --> 00:14:51.877
See, I missed the room.

00:14:56.609 --> 00:14:58.570
Oh, hello.
Excuse me...

00:15:01.861 --> 00:15:03.647
Don't come near my room.

00:15:03.731 --> 00:15:07.811
Why did you just punch me?
I apologized, haven't I?

00:15:09.819 --> 00:15:12.521
Wait! You hurt my face!

00:15:14.197 --> 00:15:15.332
Wait!

00:15:15.443 --> 00:15:21.210
-Stop, Archie. He's always like that.
-We have no idea what's he thinking about.

00:15:21.514 --> 00:15:23.869
I'll challenge him the next time I see him!

00:15:25.276 --> 00:15:27.888
So that's what happened...

00:15:30.638 --> 00:15:31.751
Here, Kurin.

00:15:32.433 --> 00:15:34.679
Anyway, I don't like him.

00:15:35.272 --> 00:15:36.822
Me, too!

00:15:37.657 --> 00:15:39.644
Candy, something happened to you?

00:15:40.545 --> 00:15:42.382
Huh? A little...

00:15:42.561 --> 00:15:47.493
Come to think of it, what happened to the letter
for Archie that was mistakenly delivered to our ward?

00:15:47.528 --> 00:15:49.609
Huh... it's here.

00:15:50.849 --> 00:15:53.254
-Was it this letter?
-That's the one!

00:15:53.444 --> 00:15:55.995
You haven't read it yet, Archie?

00:15:56.507 --> 00:15:59.270
That's right. This Archie guy,
he's totally freaking over it.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:00.511
Give it, brother!

00:16:00.546 --> 00:16:03.890
If you really don't want to read this
letter, why don't you dump it then?

00:16:04.377 --> 00:16:06.116
That's fine with me!

00:16:08.961 --> 00:16:10.448
He can't do that!

00:16:10.873 --> 00:16:13.347
Say, who wrote it to him?

00:16:13.878 --> 00:16:17.065
To beloved mr. Archie...
...from Annie Brighton.

00:16:17.292 --> 00:16:18.302
Stop that!

00:16:19.186 --> 00:16:20.377
Annie...?

00:16:21.433 --> 00:16:24.260
Yes! She writes to him every week!

00:16:24.492 --> 00:16:26.241
Really?

00:16:29.366 --> 00:16:34.033
Annie is... she is sending letters
to Archie every week.

00:16:35.726 --> 00:16:38.918
Archie, why won't you read Annie's letter?

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.939
I don't want to read it.

00:16:41.485 --> 00:16:44.703
Anyway, it seems as if Annie
wants to transfer to this school.

00:16:45.629 --> 00:16:47.530
Annie wants to...

00:16:50.387 --> 00:16:51.837
Open the door.

00:16:52.275 --> 00:16:54.258
It's the teacher patrol!

00:16:54.991 --> 00:16:56.275
What'll I do...

00:16:56.488 --> 00:16:58.122
Hurry, to the next room!

00:17:06.332 --> 00:17:08.980
-Archibald Cornwell.
-Yes!

00:17:09.015 --> 00:17:12.220
-Alistear Cornwell.
-Yes!

00:17:13.608 --> 00:17:17.679
Lights-off time has passed already.
Just what were you doing in here?

00:17:17.902 --> 00:17:21.450
Uh.. you see, we noticed that the moon in
London is somewhat different from the moon

00:17:21.451 --> 00:17:24.561
...we saw in America so now we're discussing
how it's possible from a a scientific point of view...

00:17:24.562 --> 00:17:26.049
Because the moon in America...

00:17:26.409 --> 00:17:29.245
One... two... three.

00:17:30.276 --> 00:17:33.876
Uh, I was drinking two cups...

00:17:34.074 --> 00:17:36.128
Take a look in the neighboring room.

00:17:38.401 --> 00:17:39.656
Candy...!

00:17:52.286 --> 00:17:55.590
Candy isn't the kind of girl
who just hides quietly.

00:17:56.711 --> 00:17:59.684
Kurin, if Annie really comes...

00:18:01.939 --> 00:18:05.265
That's right. We won't be able
to be too personal with her.

00:18:06.688 --> 00:18:11.856
It's because Annie wouldn't like people to know
that both she and I used to live together in Pony's home.

00:18:11.891 --> 00:18:16.039
Maybe I would've fared better if I did like Annie
and kept silent about my past in Pony's home.

00:18:19.636 --> 00:18:24.317
My life in Pony's home gave Eliza
and others a reason to ridicule me.

00:18:27.758 --> 00:18:30.072
That inverted envelope is one of those
things, too.

00:18:30.793 --> 00:18:35.679
It seems that I'll learn how Annie felt
when she had to hide our friendship.

00:18:36.702 --> 00:18:40.060
Oh, no! Patty is still waiting for me!

00:18:41.118 --> 00:18:44.139
Kurin, I'm going back to my room.
Good night.

00:18:51.357 --> 00:18:53.253
I'm so sorry, Patty!

00:18:54.192 --> 00:18:56.942
A teacher patrol suddenly barged in,
I couldn't pick up the chocolate...

00:18:56.977 --> 00:19:00.339
No, I waited here because I have to apologize to you.

00:19:00.601 --> 00:19:02.820
What do you want to apologize for?

00:19:03.254 --> 00:19:08.511
-I made a stupid mistake.
-A mistake?

00:19:09.089 --> 00:19:11.106
That letter...

00:19:13.918 --> 00:19:17.292
I saw it in that inverted envelope...
...and I...

00:19:17.327 --> 00:19:19.824
What, I don't care if you read it!

00:19:19.859 --> 00:19:23.821
There aren't any secrets or nasty stuff
in that letter!

00:19:25.968 --> 00:19:27.515
It made me cry!

00:19:29.966 --> 00:19:33.117
I was so jealous of you!

00:19:33.545 --> 00:19:35.060
Of me?

00:19:35.097 --> 00:19:37.542
Whenever I read a letter,

00:19:37.577 --> 00:19:40.292
...I try to imagine the sender
as the letter was being written.

00:19:40.327 --> 00:19:42.768
-At the moment of writing?
-Yes!

00:19:45.606 --> 00:19:48.437
Carefully taking apart an used envelope,

00:19:48.472 --> 00:19:51.402
...flipping it inside-out into a new envelope
while sending you a piece of her heart.

00:19:51.566 --> 00:19:54.034
I was envisioning that person.

00:19:57.496 --> 00:20:00.864
That's what sister Pony does
after all the children fall asleep.

00:20:00.899 --> 00:20:05.667
-I'm so happy that you got such a letter!
-Thank you, Patty!

00:20:05.994 --> 00:20:12.544
I was stupid! Up until a moment ago,
I hated this overturned envelope!

00:20:13.346 --> 00:20:16.656
If you did that, God would have punished you!

00:20:17.074 --> 00:20:21.006
-I knew you'd understand, Patty!
-I'm not the only one!

00:20:21.041 --> 00:20:25.833
-Sister Margaret understood, too!
-That's why she punished Eliza!

00:20:28.307 --> 00:20:32.187
If you truly have a heart, you'll
understand the hearts of others!

00:20:36.167 --> 00:20:37.246
Patty!

00:20:40.880 --> 00:20:44.948
The one bearing a heart
can understand the hearts of others.

00:20:45.527 --> 00:20:47.949
That's exactly what Candy thought.

00:20:50.556 --> 00:20:54.322
However, there was one heart
that Candy could not understand.

00:20:55.423 --> 00:20:57.498
It was Terry's heart.

00:20:58.190 --> 00:21:01.425
Behind his violent exterior, just what
kind of person was Terry?

00:21:01.731 --> 00:21:06.117
No matter how much she thought,
he remained a mystery.

00:21:16.507 --> 00:21:20.073
To be continued.
